**LCC Timeline
1999 - Greater London Authority Act provides mayor with power to introduce Road User Charging
2000 - Ken Livingstone elected as mayor with congestion charging part of manifesto
2003 - February LCC introduced at £5 per day
2005 - Fee increased to £8
2007 - Feb western extension introduced
2011 - Jan wester extension removed

**Spatial Regression Models
For the models, I needed to remove some observations:
    E00023812 & E00022974 - are neighbourless, which causes problems for the creating of the spatial weights matrix
    
**Spatial Weights Issue
There are a few different ways to create spatial weights, [1] contiguity, [2] distance, [3] K-nearest
For distance, the minimum bandwidth to ensure no neighbourless cases is 555.009860
K-nearest based on the mode number from contiguity, being 4
Binary spatial weights are also being created 

